        "backgroundField": "Dr. Anatoliy Rudin is a distinguished endocrine surgeon and Assistant Professor in the Department of Surgery, Division of Surgical Oncology. With a specialization in the treatment of thyroid, parathyroid, and adrenal diseases, Dr. Rudin brings a wealth of experience and expertise to his practice. He completed his General Surgery residency at the Mayo Clinic in Rochester, MN, followed by an Endocrine Surgery Fellowship at the Cleveland Clinic in Cleveland, OH. Dr. Rudin's research interest is dedicated to improving surgical outcomes through the integration of emerging technologies, advanced imaging, and minimally invasive techniques. His contributions to the field are well-documented through multiple publications and book chapters. Additionally, he has extensive leadership experience and holds committee responsibilities with organizations, including the American Association of Endocrine Surgeons. In his clinical practice, Dr. Rudin provides comprehensive surgical evaluations for patients with endocrine disorders and cancer. He employs a variety of diagnostic techniques, including ultrasound, fine needle aspiration, cytology, and molecular testing, to ensure accurate diagnosis and assessment. Dr. Rudin is adept in the latest surgical techniques, including robotic surgery, and offers personalized treatment options for thyroid, parathyroid, and adrenal diseases. He is committed to a holistic approach to patient care, working closely with individuals to develop tailored treatment plans that address their unique needs. Currently, Dr. Rudin sees patients at the Johns Hopkins Howard County Medical Center To support Dr. Rudin's research, visit: https://secure.jhu.edu/form/Rudin",
